  "note": [
    "bard's curated transcription models.",
    "",
    "This is data, not decoration. `architecture` is what tells the loader which",
    "engine a model belongs to, and nothing in a model's own files states it",
    "reliably. Adding a model means adding a row here, not a branch in the loader.",
    "",
    "`accuracy`, `speed`, and `value` are 0-100 and deliberately coarse. They",
    "help someone choose without knowing what a mel spectrogram is, and they",
    "are relative to the other rows in this file, not to any benchmark.",
    "",
    "Every row records the exact conversion repository and revision that produced",
    "the bytes, the upstream model and licence, and the pinned Bard release",
    "that serves the file. The file's own SHA-256 and byte size are verified",
    "before the engine is allowed to activate it."
